\b 1. Purpose\b0\par
Internal read-only tooling to audit Google Ads campaign spend, list active/paused campaigns, and verify manager/user access after agency offboarding. Supports Merchant/Google channel operations for our e-commerce (stretch ceiling profiles, PL market).\par
\par
\b 2. Architecture\b0\par
- Private repository: alumineu-channel-google\par
- Runtime: Node.js 20+\par
- Library: google-ads-api (official Google Ads API client)\par
- Auth: OAuth 2.0 desktop flow; refresh token stored locally (token-ads.json); not committed to git\par
- GCP project: oceanic-craft-452806-c0 (same as Merchant API)\par
- Developer token: MCC 1145409300\par
\par
\b 3. API usage\b0\par
- GAQL queries: customer, campaign, metrics (cost_micros, clicks, impressions), customer_user_access, customer_manager_link\par
- No mutations in phase 1 (no campaign create/update/bid changes)\par
- Estimated volume: under 100 API calls per day; manual/scheduled audits only\par
\par
\b 4. Users\b0\par
Internal employees only (1-2 people). No external or client access.\par
\par
\b 5. Data handling\b0\par
Credentials in local .env and token-ads.json. No third-party SaaS. No sale or sharing of Google Ads data.\par
\par
\b 6. Scripts\b0\par
- ads:auth — OAuth token acquisition\par
- ads:verify — list accessible customers\par
- ads:audit — campaign spend and access audit\par
